  "key_result": "The AA/BB sector IS finite when the spectral sum is reorganized to respect the factor heat-kernel structure. The coincident-factor sum Phi(t) diverges as t^{-3}, but the separated-factor sum Psi(t) contains the off-diagonal heat kernel at the antipode, which provides exponential suppression exp(-pi^2/(2t)) that defeats the polynomial divergence. The product Phi*Psi is integrable.",
