  "why_naive_diverged": "The naive mode-by-mode sum evaluates the coincident-factor (A) harmonics first, giving a divergent partial sum ~L^4. This is because summing over l_A at fixed l_B accumulates the diagonal singularity without the off-diagonal suppression from the B factor. The reorganized computation keeps both factors in their heat-kernel form, allowing the off-diagonal B-kernel to suppress the diagonal A-singularity."
